    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`.\n\n**Format** \u2014 `memberId = REGION + FY + HASH8 + CHK` where:\n- `REGION` \u2014 region code from postcode (range first, city fallback)\n- `FY` \u2014 2-digit fiscal year of the registrationDate (`startYear % 100`)\n- `HASH8` \u2014 first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName` (the same digest used elsewhere)\n- `CHK` \u2014 single Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 renamed `customerCode`/`customer_code` field + getter/setter to `memberId`/`member_id`.\n2. **`schema.sql`** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` (widened to `VARCHAR(32)` to fit the longer format).\n3. **`AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2192 `AssignMemberId.java`** \u2014 computes the unified `memberId`; collision handling now scans/de-dupes against existing `memberId`s (appending `-<n>`). Updated the `owners.POST.yml` step and its inbound `next:` reference.\n4. **`Localities.java`** \u2014 `region(Owner)` now recovers REGION from the `memberId`'s leading letter run (before the FY digits) instead of splitting a `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code.\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 dropped `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings; added a direct `memberId` mapping. `fiscalYear` unchanged.\n6. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 audit line now logs `memberId` (id, registrationDate, membershipLevel retained); removed the `membershipNumber` helper.\n7. **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 `primaryIdentifier` and the record field now carry `memberId`.\n8. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schemas; added `memberId` (regenerates `OwnerDto` accordingly).\n9. **`CheckDigits.java`** \u2014 refreshed javadoc (still used for the CHK segment).\n\nThe old fields are fully removed from the API surface, and collision handling, the audit line, the structured event, and the owner locality all reference the `memberId`.",
